    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into matchup-dependent upside, anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (79.66) and **Josh Naylor** (72.02). **Corbin Carroll** is our highest-projected asset today; despite a platoon disadvantage against Quintana, the matchup against a 5.24 xERA arm combined with his elite sprint speed makes him a must-start and a prime candidate for a multi-steal game. **Josh Naylor** remains a cornerstone of the middle order, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Lugo to drive production in our power categories. We are also monitoring the status of **James Wood** (69.92); assuming he confirms the leadoff spot, his combination of a 0.379 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez makes him an elite play. **Zach McKinstry** also earns a nod today (65.79), bolstered by an aggressive +16% park factor adjustment that pushes him ahead of safer, lower-ceiling options.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly rigorous today, with **Jose Caballero** (47.06) serving as the closest cut. While **Jose Caballero** remains an intriguing dart throw due to the 91% stolen base suppression rate of his opponent, he was ultimately benched because his negative platoon splits against Rasmussen and a poor spot in the order diluted his efficiency score compared to the upside of **Travis Bazzana** or **Cole Young**. We must exercise caution with **Brice Turang** (49.06); while his batting order spot is beneficial, he faces Yamamoto, whose ability to neutralize base stealers presents a significant risk to his primary value proposition. Furthermore, we are keeping a close watch on **Austin Riley** (52.57) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (56.94), both of whom are in marginal territory; **Vinnie Pasquantino** relies heavily on a +14% platoon advantage, but the 3.42 xERA of his opponent, Woo, keeps his ceiling firmly capped. We continue to hold **Mickey Moniak** on the IL, hoping for his return to bolster our bench depth, while **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** remain stashed in reserve as we navigate the scarcity of this 5x5 landscape.",
